/**
 * Colorado Contracts and Regulations (48 classroom hours) — module question bank.
 *
 * THE COURSE NO APPLICANT ESCAPES. C.R.S. § 12-10-203(4)(b) relieves an applicant licensed as a BROKER in
 * another jurisdiction of everything except this course and Real Estate Closings. § 12-10-203(4)(c) relieves
 * an applicant licensed as a SALESPERSON elsewhere of everything except this course and the whole 72-hour
 * group. EVERY APPLICANT COMPLETES THESE 48 HOURS, whatever they hold elsewhere — which is the closest
 * Colorado analogue to Arizona's 27-hour unwaivable block, and it is a different shape: Arizona's is a
 * state-specific block inside the 90; Colorado's is an entire named course.
 *
 * WRITTEN TO THE COMMISSION'S OWN OUTLINE, approved 6 June 1996 and updated 07/03/06, whose five topics
 * carry the Commission's hours: 8, 4, 16, 16, 4 = 48 — with the outline's own footnote that III and IV are
 * "Approximate hours; together must total 32 hours."
 *
 * TOPIC II IS BUILT ON SECTION NUMBERS THE COMMISSION ITSELF LISTS. It is the only topic across the six
 * outlines whose sub-topics are statute sections: §§ 12-10-402 through 12-10-411, named one by one. Module
 * 02 delivers them in that order.
 *
 * THE OUTLINE'S OWN COMPLETION REQUIREMENTS, which are not satisfied by reading:
 *   Topic III — "Students must complete a minimum of one of each of the 6 FAMILIES of listing and buyer
 *               brokerage contracts ... In addition, students must complete ONE OF EACH TYPE OF THE RELATED
 *               FORMS."
 *   Topic IV  — "Students must complete a minimum of one of each of the 4 FAMILIES of sales contracts and
 *               complete one of each of the related forms. Include examples of NEW FINANCING, LOAN
 *               ASSUMPTION, and OWNER CARRY FINANCING."
 * The engine records each completed form separately and does not credit this course without them. NO ITEM
 * IN THIS BANK MAY SUGGEST THAT READING SUBSTITUTES FOR COMPLETING A FORM.
 *
 * THE LARGEST SUBMISSION GATE IN THE COLORADO BUILD. § 12-10-403(4)(c) and Rule 7.1.A require a broker to
 * "use a Commission-approved form when such a form exists and is appropriate for the transaction", and Rule
 * 7.1.A directs the broker to the Division's website to obtain them. NO COMMISSION-APPROVED FORM WAS
 * OBTAINED, READ OR REPRODUCED BY THIS PROJECT. No item states any form's contents, version, date,
 * paragraph numbering or provisions.
 *
 * Each module carries one applied item, five engagement items and five remediation items. The correct
 * answer is authored at index 0 and permuted deterministically per item id at delivery. The public delivery
 * path strips correctChoice and rationale, and a test proves it. The 80 percent engagement threshold and
 * 100 percent applied threshold are STATECOURSE STANDARDS; the Commission's outline requires that "testing
 * is required," and these items are NOT that test.
 *
 * WHAT WAS NOT READ, AND WHICH THEREFORE APPEARS IN NO ITEM: every Commission-approved form; every
 * Commission position statement; the Conway-Bogue decision and Colorado Bar Association v. The Title
 * Guaranty Company, both named by the outline at Topic I.B; Colorado's statute of frauds; the Uniform Power
 * of Attorney Act; any Colorado electronic transactions statute; Title 12 Article 10 Parts 5 through 8
 * including the subdivision, conversion and time share provisions; the Colorado Fair Housing Act; the
 * Appraiser Licensing Act and § 12-10-602; the Colorado Common Interest Ownership Act; §§ 12-10-217,
 * 12-10-219, 12-10-222, 12-10-218 and 12-10-304; § 38-35.5-101; § 38-12-101 et seq.; § 38-35-125; the
 * Commission's Transaction File Checklist; Colorado's foreclosure and public trustee statutes; its water
 * law, mechanics' lien, recording, special district, surveying and property tax statutes; the U.C.C.C.; and
 * RESPA.
 *
 * Course version 1.0 submission draft — NOT APPROVED. No Colorado qualifying education hours are available.
 */

